+# Content 0.5.5 — complete unlock audit
+
+Baseline: `423e1ec006315b1fdc3ec8b96d9fc00525b32490`. All 16 evidence items (including six references) and all three procedure/task records are covered. No items were cut. Four narration lines were added from existing card bodies verbatim; no existing dialogue was edited. No start exemptions are used.
+
+This table specifies intended post-integration visibility. The standard dialogue sheet inventories the candidate against the baseline renderer, which does not yet consume unlocked_by. It verifies wording coverage, not R2 timing.
+
+| ID | unlocked_by | Presenting line / scene | Why |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `g8-ev-rule` | `{"line":"g8-line-rcs-termination"}` | `g8-stabilization-report.lines[0]` — They've regained control using the reentry thrusters. They've used substantial propellant from both RCS rings. That means we terminate the mission. | Mara explicitly reports both RCS rings, substantial use and mission termination. Earlier briefing acquisition is internal only; do not expose the title. The earlier optional crew relay does not unlock this card. |
+| `g8-ev-contact-primer` | `{"node":"g8-loss-of-contact"}` | `g8-loss-of-contact.text` — The scheduled tracking pass has ended. There's no new report from the spacecraft. | The scheduled pass has ended and no new report is available. R2 explicitly selects this loss-of-contact scene; not the briefing or preparation option that cites the primer. |
+| `g8-ev-contact-worksheet` | `{"preparation":"g8-prep-contact"}` | `g8-prep-select.text + selected option g8-prep-contact` — In the contact drill, Houston CAPCOM and a tracking-ship CAPCOM practice sending an instruction, reading it back, and confirming receipt to FLIGHT. In the recovery drill, Elias and the Department of Defense recovery coordinator practice passing the aircraft's location report to the ship and confirming who sends the pickup instruction. In the systems drill, Mara calls a low-propellant warning to FLIGHT and CAPCOM together, then passes her recommended response before the next entry task begins. Selected: Rehearse sending an instruction and confirming its receipt. | Only the selected contact rehearsal produces this worksheet. Reading the menu is not selecting the drill. |
+| `g8-ev-recovery-worksheet` | `{"preparation":"g8-prep-recovery"}` | `g8-prep-select.text + selected option g8-prep-recovery` — In the contact drill, Houston CAPCOM and a tracking-ship CAPCOM practice sending an instruction, reading it back, and confirming receipt to FLIGHT. In the recovery drill, Elias and the Department of Defense recovery coordinator practice passing the aircraft's location report to the ship and confirming who sends the pickup instruction. In the systems drill, Mara calls a low-propellant warning to FLIGHT and CAPCOM together, then passes her recommended response before the next entry task begins. Selected: Rehearse passing the pickup instruction from the recovery desk to the ship. | Apply the same selected-rehearsal rule to the third worksheet; it must never appear on a run without recovery preparation. |
